# Translation copy

User-facing text comes from every file in `i18n/locales/`. All locale files stay in lockstep.

- In Vue and composables, call `t()` from `useShopI18n()`. It fills `{name}`, `{subtitle}`, and `{email}` from `site.config.ts`.
- Internal links use `NuxtLinkLocale` with an unprefixed path such as `/shop`. Plain `NuxtLink` drops the Dutch prefix. The language switcher is the exception: it already receives a localized path from `useSwitchLocalePath()`.
- Do not use `$t()` and do not pass a variable into `t()`.
- Product, collection, and badge copy uses the keys already scanned by `pnpm check:i18n`.
- In message text, write a literal `@` as `{'@'}`. The `@` character is vue-i18n syntax.
- The shop name and Chinese subtitle stay in `site.config.ts`. Language names stay on the locale objects in `nuxt.config.ts`, written in that language.
- Prices, stock, and image paths stay in `server/data/catalog.ts`.

```vue
<!-- Use the helper -->
{{ t('hero.title') }}

<!-- A new product needs products.<slug> in every locale -->
{{ t(`products.${item.slug}.title`) }}
```

Run `pnpm check:i18n` before handing work over. `pnpm build` runs it too.
